// portfolio.cpp -- linear-algebra portfolio analysis with live price updates.
//
// C++17, no external libraries. Live prices come from the system `curl`
// command (Yahoo Finance chart endpoint, via popen). Linear algebra
// (Gaussian elimination, Jacobi eigen-solver) is implemented below.
//
// Build:   g++ -O2 -std=c++17 portfolio.cpp -o portfolio
// History: a CSV with header "Date,QQQ,NVDA,..." and one row per trading day
//          (oldest first, adjusted closes). Columns not in TICKERS are treated
//          as candidates for the "other stocks" recommendations. Make one with:
//            python -c "import yfinance as yf; yf.download(['QQQ','ANT','NVDA',
//            'GH','SPCX','MRNA','TRI','VKTX','YU.L','SPY','SCHD','PG','JNJ',
//            'TLT','GLD','BRK-B'],period='3y',auto_adjust=True)['Close']
//            .to_csv('prices.csv')"
// Run:
//   ./portfolio --csv prices.csv --interval 60 --value 25000
//   ./portfolio --csv prices.csv --once                (analysis only)
//   ./portfolio --csv prices.csv --shares "NVDA=10,QQQ=5,YU.L=500"
//   ./portfolio --demo --interval 1 --iterations 3     (offline test)
//
// Not financial advice. Free data is delayed; don't poll faster than ~30 s.

